516 0 obj
<<
/Title (Beak morphology directly determines feeding success and survival. Large, broad beaks generate the crushing force needed to crack hard seeds in seed-rich, arid environments. Narrow, pointed beaks efficiently manipulate smaller and softer seeds in other habitats. Long cactus-beaks allow birds to reach deep into cactus flowers to access nectar and pollen in dry zones. \(Abzhanov, 2010; Clark et al., 2020\))
