592 0 obj
<<
/Title (Genetic Drift Random changes in allele frequencies occur independently of natural selection. This effect is amplified in small, isolated island populations, where chance events can rapidly shift the genetic composition of a finch population.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 589 0 R
/Next 594 0 R
>>
endobj
593 0 obj
<<
/Title (Gene Flow Alleles move between populations through migration and hybridization. Interbreeding between finch populations on different islands transfers genetic variants, increasing diversity and influencing evolutionary trajectories.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 589 0 R
/Prev 594 0 R
>>
endobj
594 0 obj
<<
/Title (Mutation New genetic variants are introduced through mutations in DNA. Some mutations affect key genes such as ALX1 and HMGA2, directly influencing beak shape and size and providing raw material for evolutionary change.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 589 0 R
/Prev 592 0 R
/Next 593 0 R
>>
endobj
